{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$root='\"'C:\\\\Users\\\\Andrew\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\C--code-claude-plugin-marketplace\\\\820981ec-d49f-44af-8417-8c4b11abf226\\\\scratchpad\\\\mgs-review\\\\shards'; Get-Content -Raw (Join-Path \"'$root '\"'001-plugins_slack-bridge_CONFIG.md-e9a76746.diff'); Get-Content -Raw (Join-Path \"'$root '\"'002-plugins_slack-bridge_README.md-3cb278a1.diff'); Get-Content -Raw (Join-Path \"'$root '\"'003-plugins_slack-bridge_assets_slack-app-manifest.yaml-edf8f88e.diff'); Get-Content -Raw (Join-Path \"'$root '\"'004-plugins_slack-bridge_src_config.mjs-365d99b6.diff'); Get-Content -Raw (Join-Path \"'$root '\"'005-plugins_slack-bridge_src_core_claude-subprocess.mjs-46b6054d.diff')\"","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/plugins/slack-bridge/CONFIG.md b/plugins/slack-bridge/CONFIG.md\nindex 9730fda..efa7eaf 100644\n--- a/plugins/slack-bridge/CONFIG.md\n+++ b/plugins/slack-bridge/CONFIG.md\n@@ -30,46 +30,44 @@ For production deployments, prefer env vars for token values so they don't land\n \n ## Model routing\n \n-The bridge agent runs on your Claude Code default model unless `claude.model` is set. Any non-Claude model name (e.g. an ollama `:cloud` tag) routes through the Anthropic-format endpoint in `proxy` — same mechanism as the pipeline plugin; the auth token is a pass-through placeholder (ollama auth rides the app's ambient signin). Change the config, restart the bridge, job done.\n+Each channel picks its own model with `/model <name>` in Slack. Until it does, a message in an unclaimed channel gets a one-line hint and spawns nothing. Thread sessions use their channel's model. `/new` clears the session and keeps the model.\n+\n+Any non-Claude model name (e.g. an ollama `:cloud` tag) routes through the Anthropic-format endpoint in `proxy` — same mechanism as the pipeline plugin; the auth token is a pass-through placeholder (ollama auth rides the app's ambient signin). Switching a channel between a Claude and a non-Claude model drops its session, since neither side can resume the other's.\n \n ```json\n {\n-  \"claude\": {\n-    \"cwd\": \"/home/user/myproject\",\n-    \"model\": \"minimax-m3:cloud\"\n-  },\n   \"proxy\": {\n     \"url\": \"http://localhost:11434\",\n     \"authToken\": \"ollama\"\n   }\n }\n ```\n \n-Defaults: `claude.model` null (Claude default); `proxy.url` `http://localhost:11434`; `proxy.authToken` `\"ollama\"`. Claude models (`claude-*`, `haiku`, `sonnet`, `opus`, `fable`) never touch the proxy. The heartbeat's `slack.verbModel` is independent and stays on Claude.\n+Defaults: `proxy.url` `http://localhost:11434`; `proxy.authToken` `\"ollama\"`. Claude models (`claude-*`, `haiku`, `sonnet`, `opus`, `fable`) never touch the proxy. The heartbeat's `slack.verbModel` is independent and stays on Claude. Existing Slack app installs must re-apply the app manifest before `/model` appears in the client.\n \n ## Remote control\n \n `remote` configures the optional remote-control subsystem — see README → *Remote control* for the operator-facing flow. Remote control is **off** unless `remote.controlToken` is set (the `claude-slack setup` wizard writes it for you).\n \n ```json\n {\n   \"remote\": {\n     \"controlToken\": \"shared-secret-here\",\n     \"brokerPort\": 7898,\n     \"controlPort\": 7897,\n     \"createChannels\": false,\n     \"operatorUserId\": \"U0123ABC\",\n     \"replyTimeoutMs\": 300000\n   }\n }\n ```\n \n | Key | Default | Notes |\n |-----|---------|-------|\n | `remote.controlToken` | `null` | Shared-secret bearer token guarding the localhost control endpoint and the broker's state-touching routes (`/health` stays open for liveness probes). `null` disables remote control. The wizard generates one when left blank. |\n | `remote.brokerPort` | `7898` | Internal localhost broker port. Distinct from `claude-peers`' 7899 on purpose, so the two subsystems don't collide if both run. Token-guarded like the control endpoint when `controlToken` is set. |\n | `remote.controlPort` | `7897` | Internal localhost control endpoint port. Localhost-only; the token is the auth boundary. |\n | `remote.createChannels` | `false` | `true` → `/remote` creates `#rc-<context-slug>` (requires `channels:write` + `channels:manage` on the bot token). `false` → DM-seize (no new scopes). |\n | `remote.operatorUserId` | `null` | The operator's Slack user id. With `createChannels` it is invited into each new `#rc-<context>` channel — without it the channel is created with only the bot in it. Without `createChannels` it selects which DM the DM-seize fallback seizes — unset, DM-seize **refuses** rather than guessing at a DM. The wizard asks for it. |\n | `remote.replyTimeoutMs` | `300000` | Per-message: how long the bridge waits for the live session's reply before posting \"live session didn't reply in time\". The claim is retained across a timeout (peer may be slow, not dead). Stretched to 12× while an `AskUserQuestion` dialog is open in the session. 300 s is generous headroom for a session that has to wake, read the message and answer; shorten it only if you want the timeout notice sooner. |\n | `remote.heartbeatIntervalMs` | `15000` | How often the session-side MCP server heartbeats its peer registration so the broker's liveness view stays current. |\n\r\ndiff --git a/plugins/slack-bridge/README.md b/plugins/slack-bridge/README.md\nindex 42b88e3..1bb7b64 100644\n--- a/plugins/slack-bridge/README.md\n+++ b/plugins/slack-bridge/README.md\n@@ -161,14 +161,15 @@ claude-slack import-sessions <file.json>             Import sessions from anothe\n claude-slack --help                                  Show this help\n ```\n \n **In Slack:**\n \n | Command | Effect |\n |---------|--------|\n | `/new` or `/reset` | Clear session, start fresh |\n | `/stop` | Kill in-flight Claude subprocess |\n | `/restart` | Restart the bridge daemon |\n+| `/model <name>` | Pick the model this channel spawns; no argument shows it. A channel with no model gets a hint and spawns nothing |\n \n ---\n \n ## Configuration reference\n@@ -176,22 +177,21 @@ claude-slack --help                                  Show this help\n Edit `config.json` (path shown in Step 3 above) to adjust any of these:\n \n | Key | Default | Description |\n |-----|---------|-------------|\n | `tokens.bot` | *(required)* | Bot OAuth token (`xoxb-...`) |\n | `tokens.app` | *(required)* | App-level token (`xapp-...`) for Socket Mode |\n | `claude.cwd` | *(required)* | Working directory for `claude -p` invocations |\n | `claude.addDir` | `null` | Extra `--add-dir` path passed to claude |\n-| `claude.model` | `null` | Agent model. `null` = Claude Code default. Claude names pass as `--model`; any other name (e.g. `minimax-m3:cloud`) routes via `proxy` — see [CONFIG.md](CONFIG.md) \"Model routing\" |\n | `proxy.url` | `http://localhost:11434` | Anthropic-format endpoint for non-Claude models (ollama direct) |\n | `proxy.authToken` | `\"ollama\"` | Pass-through placeholder — real auth is the ollama app's signin |\n | `claude.timeout` | `180000` | Subprocess timeout in ms |\n | `slack.onlyChannel` | `null` | If set, only respond in this channel ID |\n | `slack.historyLimit` | `0` | Messages to fetch for context bootstrap (0 = disabled) |\n | `slack.notifyChannel` | `null` | Channel for `claude-slack notify` when `--channel` is omitted |\n | `slack.sessionKey` | `\"channel-thread\"` | `\"channel\"` or `\"channel-thread\"` |\n | `slack.verbMode` | `\"static\"` | `\"static\"` (fallback verbs) or `\"haiku\"` (LLM-generated verbs) |\n | `extensions` | `[]` | Paths to ESM extension modules |\n \n ---\n \n ## Remote control (optional)\n\r\ndiff --git a/plugins/slack-bridge/assets/slack-app-manifest.yaml b/plugins/slack-bridge/assets/slack-app-manifest.yaml\nindex de2f672..1883193 100644\n--- a/plugins/slack-bridge/assets/slack-app-manifest.yaml\n+++ b/plugins/slack-bridge/assets/slack-app-manifest.yaml\n@@ -6,12 +6,13 @@ display_information:\n features:\n   bot_user:\n     display_name: Claude\n     always_online: true\n   slash_commands:\n     - { command: /new,     description: Start a fresh session in this channel }\n     - { command: /reset,   description: Alias for /new }\n     - { command: /restart, description: Restart the bridge daemon }\n     - { command: /stop,    description: Interrupt Claude mid-response }\n+    - { command: /model,   description: Pick the model this channel spawns (no arg shows it) }\n \n oauth_config:\n   scopes:\n\r\ndiff --git a/plugins/slack-bridge/src/config.mjs b/plugins/slack-bridge/src/config.mjs\nindex 992343c..f64f185 100644\n--- a/plugins/slack-bridge/src/config.mjs\n+++ b/plugins/slack-bridge/src/config.mjs\n@@ -3,31 +3,30 @@ import { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n const DEFAULTS = {\n   claude: {\n     addDir: null,\n     timeout: 180_000,\n-    model: null,\n   },\n   proxy: {\n     url: \"http://localhost:11434\",\n     authToken: \"ollama\",\n   },\n   slack: {\n     onlyChannel: null,\n     historyLimit: 0,\n     notifyChannel: null,\n     sessionKey: \"channel-thread\",\n     verbMode: \"static\",\n     verbModel: \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n   },\n   extensions: [],\n   remote: {\n     brokerPort: 7898,\n     controlPort: 7897,\n     controlToken: null,\n     createChannels: false,\n     operatorUserId: null,\n     // Long enough for a session that has to wake, read the message and answer.\n     // A reply that lands after the window is still posted to the claimed channel.\n     replyTimeoutMs: 300_000,\n     heartbeatIntervalMs: 15_000,\n   },\n };\n\r\ndiff --git a/plugins/slack-bridge/src/core/claude-subprocess.mjs b/plugins/slack-bridge/src/core/claude-subprocess.mjs\nindex a150c2e..7f3655b 100644\n--- a/plugins/slack-bridge/src/core/claude-subprocess.mjs\n+++ b/plugins/slack-bridge/src/core/claude-subprocess.mjs\n@@ -2,11 +2,11 @@ import { spawn } from \"node:child_process\";\n \n const CLAUDE_ALIASES = new Set([\"haiku\", \"sonnet\", \"opus\", \"fable\"]);\n \n-function isClaudeModel(model) {\n+export function isClaudeModel(model) {\n   return model.startsWith(\"claude-\") || CLAUDE_ALIASES.has(model.toLowerCase());\n }\n \n // Windows NT status codes (0xC0000000+) arrive as large positive exit numbers.\n // Name the common loader/exec failures so a crash like 0xC0000135 isn't an\n // opaque \"3221225786\" in the Slack error reply — the operator can act on\n // \"STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND\" where a bare number is meaningless.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
